Subject: internal/runtime/atomic: implement the atomics with the threads
 proposal's instructions
Last-Update: 2026-10-04

The wasm port's atomic operations were plain loads and stores, correct
on one thread only. With GOWASM=threads the package implements them
with the threads proposal's atomic instructions, sequentially
consistent as the proposal defines them, so that the runtime and
sync/atomic are correct with several threads over a shared memory.
Address 0 does not trap in wasm, so each body first checks its pointer
and raises the nil dereference panic on nil, as the compiler's check
does for the pure Go version. A function that differs from another only
in its Go types jumps to that body, as on the other ports. Without the
feature the single-threaded implementation stays.

